---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Run monitors once, store the results and exit 0 (pass), 1 (an assertion failed), 3 (a request errored) or 4 (blocked): for cron, systemd timers, launchd and CI schedules

Usage: rustman monitor run [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]
          The monitor to run (its name)

Options:
      --all
          Run every monitor of the workspace, one after the other

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
